I am now focusing on the `sw.js` file. I have a simple plan to make sure it caches important assets, and serves them if I am offline. Since this is an AI bot, I need the network, so I have a network-first strategy. I'm prioritizing getting the "Add to Home Screen" banner to trigger on Android. I've realized that the directory is treated as root, so I will add `manifest.json` and `sw.js`.


**Addressing URL Dependencies**

I'm now dealing with the URL requirements within the manifest file. While I can't generate images, I will leverage placeholder URLs for the icons, specifically referencing a CDN-hosted heart/robot image to make the PWA functional. The next step is adding an "Install App" button. I will add this to the settings or sidebar.

